{"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Destinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"],"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types","kind":"relationships"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"title":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations","generated":true}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L27","fileName":"Destination.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","title":"Destination","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order the events were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns. Batches that arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its oldest batch when full, so a destination that falls behind doesn’t hold up the others."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The delivery reports each batch dropped. Once the destination has caught up, it gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped batch’s records that a store keeps, read back from the store, after the newer batches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it received meanwhile; those kept in memory only are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" is what tells the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered"},{"text":" is set may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have reached it in an earlier run.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/docu